Input: gpio-keys: let userspace choose which buttons wake the system

Which buttons wake the system is read from the device tree once, at
probe, and nothing can change it afterwards short of editing the blob
and rebooting.  power/wakeup only turns the whole device on or off.

On the Pyra every one of its fourteen game buttons is a wakeup source,
the shoulder buttons included, so with the lid shut a shoulder button
pressed against a bag wakes the machine.  Turning power/wakeup off
stops that but also takes the face buttons and d-pad with it.

Add wakeup_keys and wakeup_switches next to disabled_keys and
disabled_switches, in the same keycode-list format.  Reading gives the
codes that wake the system; writing a list makes exactly those buttons
of that type wakeup sources.  The device tree's gpio-key,wakeup and
wakeup-source properties become the starting set, so nothing changes
until userspace writes.  The choice takes effect at the next suspend.

A device whose device tree named no wakeup button was never made wakeup
capable, so the first write that names one also makes it capable.

Masking a line that is not a wakeup source at suspend is left to the
irqchip, as before.  On OMAP the gpio driver sets
IRQCHIP_MASK_ON_SUSPEND, and masking a line also clears its bank wake
enable bit.

